      "decision": "ADMIT",
      "reason": "D03. The abstract describes email action items with explicit Action, Object, and optional Subject/agent structure and distinguishes Request, Assign, Suggest, and Deliver. That directly strengthens structured action representation and helps preserve the distinction between different action-bearing speech acts rather than extracting verbs alone.",
      "stream_id": "D03",
      "role": "DIRECT",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "paper_id": "manual-ee40d588e3",
      "decision": "ADMIT",
      "reason": "T07. The shared task explicitly annotates negation cues, scope, and focus. Scope-sensitive negation is directly transferable to determining whether an apparent action proposition is negated instead of treating the presence of an action verb as a live request or commitment.",
      "stream_id": "T07",
      "role": "TRANSFER",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "paper_id": "manual-cd3fa58e4c",
      "decision": "ADMIT",
