      "stream_id": "D06",
      "role": "DIRECT",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "paper_id": "manual-20b8cd2fdd",
      "decision": "ADMIT",
      "reason": "D06. The paper analyzes difficult real-world workplace-email request and commitment cases and proposes annotation treatments for conditional, repeated, ambiguous, and context-dependent evidence. Those phenomena map directly to the project's highest-risk false-obligation and lost-condition cases, so this materially strengthens the annotation and error model.",
      "stream_id": "D06",
      "role": "DIRECT",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
